mintcare (1.8.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * New pages: Packages (largest/installed by you/held, apt history with
    undo, kernels, mirror speed test, Mint upgrade check), Processes,
    Troubleshoot (sound, network, printers, Bluetooth, crashes), Backup
    (rsync hard-linked snapshots, schedule, settings export/import) and an
    optional Claude assistant using your own Anthropic API key.
  * Security: login audit and ClamAV/rkhunter scans with quarantine.
  * Hardware: disk and CPU benchmarks, battery health. Boot-time history.
  * Scheduled check-ups can save a health report.
  * Spanish translation; the whole interface is now translatable.
  * Accessibility: screen-reader names and live values for switches,
    gauges and charts; keyboard-driven disk-space map; shortcuts
    (Ctrl+1-9, Ctrl+Page Up/Down, F5, Ctrl+E, Ctrl+?).

